id: pm-rust-windows-artifact-cwd-parent
title: Verify ordinary Windows artifact paths before parent normalization
description: "Rust 1.90 std::path::absolute calls GetFullPathNameW for ordinary Windows paths. That call can collapse a parent component before resolve_artifact_cwd can inspect the supplied file prefix. Round GJ covers Windows verbatim paths, whose parent component reaches the Rust join. Rust reference: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/1.90.0/library/std/src/sys/path/windows.rs#L173-L195"
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: collections,follow-up,windows
created_at: "2026-11-22T12:23:22.732Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-23T10:54:43.574Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Verify the ordinary-path case in a Windows temp tracker and preserve drive-relative paths, directory aliases, and genuinely missing suffixes."
parent: pm-rust-oracle-1118
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T08:08:53.940Z",codex-sol,Round GP retains the parent component for ordinary drive-absolute paths and checks the item and history bytes on refusal. The x86_64-pc-windows-gnu cross-check passed. The regression still needs Windows runtime confirmation.
  "2026-11-23T10:54:43.574Z",codex-sol,"On f5fa7e7, the Windows shard passed the refusal and unchanged-byte assertions. It panicked after the valid directory-parent removal because the test indexed files after the last link disappeared. Round GR checks that the field is removed, as commit_mutation stores the collection. The revised assertion is pending Windows CI."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/collections.rs,project
  tests/support/collections_unit.rs,project
body: ""
